Ladybird includes both margins when deciding if an atomic inline box
fits on the current line. The fit uses the border-box inline size plus
both signed margins, so positive margins can move the box to another
line and negative margins can keep it on the current line.

Blink adds the margins from ComputeLineMarginsForVisualContainer to
the atomic inline size in LineBreaker::HandleAtomicInline. WebKit uses
InlineFormattingUtils::inlineItemWidth to obtain the margin-box width
for LineBuilder::candidateContentForLine. Gecko applies the start
margin to the frame bounds and includes the end margin in the fit
comparison in nsLineLayout::CanPlaceFrame. Ladybird follows the same
margin-box fit behavior, without changing the nowrap path.

Chrome matches the issue reductions and the controls for exact fits,
negative margins, mixed-sign margins, padding, and borders in both
left-to-right and right-to-left containers. No engine code or text was
copied into the implementation.
